      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Cast Iron contains more than 2% Carbon, rendering it hard, brittle, and excellent in damping compressive loads.",
        "Ductility allows materials to be drawn into wires, whereas Malleability enables flattening into thin sheets without rupture.",
        "Hooke's Law strictly applies only up to the Proportional Limit on the stress-strain curve."
